  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)+x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy))+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x) & =(\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(xy))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy)+1+\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}{|}_{(1/4,4)} & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4)+1+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1)+1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
